Criterion results
1. Comparison bounds, top three absolute-dollar contributors, stable category ties, no-history/no-findings: supported by B.
   Read all assertions in investigation_di4_test.go. TestDI4InvestigationRendered checks full/HX selected August and prior July bounds, rendered $100/$200; TestDI4MoneyAndContributors checks signed refund/transfer exclusion, rendered $243/$251/-$8 and Alpha/Zulu/Refund order with exactly three contributors; TestDI4EmptyHistoryRendered checks actual missing-data guidance and absent invented comparison. F proves ranking/count guards detect their intended defects.
   Independent rendered fractional probe: selected $10.01, prior $0.00, difference +$10.01 after signed refund, transfer excluded. Canonical 2.675 displays $2.67, not a new math.Round rule. Initial scratch expectation $2.68 was corrected after reading models/money.go; this was a harness error, not a finding.

2. Context, What changed, findings, recurring groups, supporting order: supported by B's ordered renderer markers, and D's actual heading lists. Both full and HX use the investigation. No repeated compatibility tiles were found in the live renderer branch.

3. Findings completeness, dedup, anchors and usable destinations: supported by B and E.
   Author assertions cover hash+type dedup (same hash/different types retained), rejection of invented/out-of-period hashes, stable reversed-input ordering, latest full-history creep anchor not pulled backward into May, and eleven detector groups including subset-name/end-day-noon fixtures.
   Independent HTTP fixture renders eleven findings in BOTH full and HX: five preview and six remaining. Every rendered finding URL was requested through the actual Explorer router and returned its actual data-hash. Not just URL parsing.
   E proves the six remaining real results are keyboard-reachable via native details in both themes. Full-history detector scope and median-versus-actual copy were inspected in the rendering templates. Existing supporting tables retain separately labeled history scope.
   F proves restoring the ten-row cap breaks the meaningful assertion.

4. Merchant-first labels, separate monthly/annual estimates, historical reference and grouping drilldowns: supported by B.
   TestCheckerDI4GroupingLinksAndPartials requests full, HX, standalone trends, recurring and income. All retain selected dates. Full/HX each follow two actual Major Expense ID links; trends follows one; recurring follows one merchant link. Explorer includes the intended selected transaction and excludes the unmatched row. ID is actual-power-id while label is Power & Light; this is not a same-name/id fixture.
   Recurring standalone contains "Expected payment estimate as of 2026-08-31"; renderer places merchant before secondary Major Expense label. Full/HX expose unmatched-outflow exclusion and non-reconciliation scope.
   Fractional renderer probe asserts grand monthly $0.02 versus independently rounded annual $0.12, shared payment precision, and no negative zero. Author group assertions cover the two displayed row estimates. F rejects raw group summation.

